@chapter 22 | Human Body Systems

@intro
This chapter goes through the human body system by system: **composition and skeleton** (water, oxygen, 206 bones, stapes, joints), **digestion** (enzymes, liver, bile, gallstones), **respiration** (alveoli, ATP), **blood and circulation** (four-chambered heart, haemoglobin, blood groups, blood pressure, pH), **excretion** (kidneys, urea, dialysis, stones), the **nervous system** (cerebellum, hypothalamus) and the **endocrine glands** and their hormones. It contains **{pyqs} PYQs and {ones} one-liners**.
@end

@section 22.1 | Composition and Skeleton

@q 39:1-2

@src 39:3
@pyq
Consider the following elements found in a normal 70 kg person and arrange them in the correct increasing order.
1. Sodium
2. Potassium
3. Copper
4. Iron
Select the correct answer using the code given below :
Code :
(a) 4, 3, 1, 2
(b) 3, 4, 2, 1
(c) 3, 4, 1, 2
(d) 4, 3, 2, 1
@ans (c)
@note The source prints no exam tag for this question and numbers "Copper" as a second item 2; it is item 3, as the codes show.
@end

The body is about **60-65% water** (a newborn about 75%). By mass the main elements are **oxygen (65%)**, carbon (18%), hydrogen (10%) and nitrogen (3%). Among minerals, **calcium** is the most abundant; a 70 kg adult has about 140 g of potassium, 100 g of sodium, 4 g of iron and only about 0.1 g of copper.

