@table
Skeleton fact | Detail
Bones in an adult | **206** (a newborn has about 270-300, which fuse)
**Smallest bone** | **Stapes** (stirrup) in the **middle ear**; with malleus and incus it carries sound
Longest / strongest bone | **Femur** (thigh)
Bone salt | Mostly **calcium phosphate** (hydroxyapatite)
**Ligament** | Joins **bone to bone**
Tendon | Joins **muscle to bone**
**Pivot joint** | Atlas and axis vertebrae: the neck turning the head
Ball-and-socket | Shoulder, hip
Hinge | Elbow, knee
**Arthroplasty** | Surgical **joint replacement** (hip, knee)
@end

