@q 39:10-13

**Calcium, phosphorus** and **fluorine** build bones and teeth; **iodine** is needed for the thyroid hormone. **Dental plaque** is a sticky film of food, saliva, acids and **bacteria**. The **masseter** (jaw) muscle can exert the greatest force for its size.

@section 22.2 | Digestion

@q 40:1-6

@table
Part | Enzyme / juice | Acts on
Mouth | **Salivary amylase (ptyalin)** | Starch → maltose
**Stomach** | **Pepsin** (with HCl), rennin (infants) | **Protein digestion begins**
Liver | **Bile** (no enzyme; stored in the **gall bladder**) | **Emulsifies fats**
Pancreas | **Trypsin**, chymotrypsin, amylase, **lipase** | Proteins, starch, fats
**Small intestine** | Maltase, sucrase, lactase, peptidases | **Most digestion and absorption**
Large intestine | - | Absorbs water; bacteria make vitamin K and B
@end

**Enzymes** are biological catalysts and are almost all **proteins**. Fat digestion needs **bile salts** and **lipase**; pepsin works on proteins only. **Pepsin** is the only one of the three enzymes released in the stomach; trypsin and chymotrypsin come from the pancreas into the small intestine.

@src 40:7
@pyq U.P.P.C.S. (Pre) 2017
Given below are two statements :
Assertion (A) : Human body is incapable of digesting cellulose.
Reason (R) : Starch degrading enzyme, diastase, is found in human body.
Choose the correct answer from the code given below:
Codes :
(a) Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).
(b) Both (A) and (R) are true but (R) is not the correct explanation of (A).
(c) (A) is true but (R) is false.
(d) (A) is false but (R) is true.
@ans (b)
@end

Humans lack **cellulase**, so cellulose passes undigested as **dietary fibre**; cows and termites digest it with the help of gut microbes. Having amylase (diastase) for starch is true but does not explain this.

