@q 45:3-5

@src1 45:2
@one
The normal temperature of the human body is
@ans 98.6°F (37°C)
@end

The **brain has no pain receptors**, so brain surgery can be done on an awake patient. Humans are **warm-blooded** (homeothermic): the hypothalamus keeps the body near **37°C** by sweating, shivering and changing blood flow.

