@q 46:3-6

@q 46:7-12

@table
Gland | Hormone | Job
**Pituitary** ("master gland", pea-sized) | Growth hormone, TSH, ACTH, FSH, LH; **ADH** and **oxytocin** (stored in the posterior lobe) | Growth; **ADH controls urine volume**; **oxytocin** for childbirth and **milk ejection** (released by hugging and suckling)
**Thyroid** | **Thyroxine** (needs **iodine**) | Metabolism; deficiency causes **goitre**
**Pancreas** (mixed gland) | **Insulin** (beta cells), glucagon (alpha cells) | Blood sugar; also secretes digestive **pancreatic juice** (the "complete digestive juice"), alkaline
**Adrenal** medulla | **Adrenaline** | **"Fight or flight"**: raises heart rate and blood sugar
Adrenal cortex | Cortisol, aldosterone | Stress, salt balance
**Pineal** | **Melatonin** | **Sleep cycle** (made in **darkness**)
Ovaries | **Estrogen** (estrone, estradiol), progesterone | Female traits, menstrual cycle, pregnancy
Testes | **Testosterone** | Male traits
Stomach / intestine | **Gastrin**, **secretin** | Gastrin: gastric juice; **secretin**: stimulates the pancreas
@end

**Insulin** is a small **protein** (51 amino acids); **oxytocin** is a short peptide (9 amino acids), so it is not counted as a protein. The pancreas is the **second largest gland** after the liver.

