@q 46:17-19

**Melatonin** is made in the **dark** and is **suppressed by bright light**, so light during sleep is undesirable; the Reason has it backwards. Human sperm stay able to fertilise for about **one to two days** (they may survive up to five days) in the female tract. The **pineal** is among the smallest endocrine glands; of the options, the source treats the **pituitary** as the smallest.

@trap
Smallest bone = **stapes** (ear). **Ligament = bone to bone.** Protein digestion **begins in the stomach** (pepsin); most digestion is in the **small intestine**. **Bile is made in the liver**, stored in the gall bladder. **Pulmonary vein carries oxygenated blood.** **O = universal donor, AB = universal recipient.** Blood pH = **7.35-7.45**. RBCs die in the **spleen**. Kidney stones = **calcium oxalate**. **Cerebellum = balance**, **hypothalamus = hunger and thirst**, **medulla = heartbeat**. **ADH** controls urine; **oxytocin** for milk ejection; **melatonin** is made in darkness. The **pancreas** is both endocrine and exocrine.
@end

@heatmap

@pattern
Human physiology questions appear every year, and the **2019-2025** papers asked several each time (pulmonary vein, pivot joint, heart chambers, blood composition, pepsin, little brain, kidney stones). The format is shifting to two-statement and "which is/are released" questions that test exact location.
@end

@next
Likely next angles: **organ donation** (NOTTO, the "Angdaan" campaign), **blood banks and thalassaemia**, **insulin pumps** and **continuous glucose monitors**, **sleep and melatonin**, **dialysis under PM-NDP** (National Dialysis Programme), **gut microbiome**, and **brain-computer interfaces**.
@end
